# The three that change the result, not just the speed:
#
#   node_modules  — a host tree (often a different platform's esbuild binary) would
#                   be used instead of the one `npm ci` installs for linux/amd64;
#   out/          — the compile fixtures are generated by `npm run build`'s
#                   prebuild step. Copying a host `out/` would make the image's
#                   provenance a lie, and staleness invisible;
#   .env          — this file is committed here, with localhost defaults. A container
#                   is configured by its environment (ConfigMap and Secret in the
#                   cluster); baking `ALLOWED_FRAME_ANCESTORS=http://localhost:3000`
#                   into an image is how a deployed sandbox ends up describing a
#                   developer's browser.
node_modules
.next
out
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

.git
.github
.husky
coverage
compile.sh
test.jsx
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
